        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(code-mode): report UTF-8 API file byte counts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCode Mode virtual API files reported JavaScript string length as `bytes`. MCP declaration files containing non-ASCII text were therefore shown with an underestimated byte count through both `API.list()` and `API.read()`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe worker now computes UTF-8 byte length at the Node host boundary before marshalling API files into QuickJS. The guest API reuses that canonical value for both list and read results.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents inspecting MCP declaration files receive accurate UTF-8 byte metadata, including declarations with internationalized descriptions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: current head `eaaa1905d195d9ce8e0a3b70e8381d6f9bc6ed56` reports UTF-8 byte counts for Code Mode MCP API virtual files through both `API.list()` and `API.read()`.\n- Real Code Mode runtime proof: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` using repo-local `createCodeModeTools()` / `applyCodeModeCatalog()` with an MCP declaration containing non-ASCII schema docs — passed with this redacted output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"head\": \"eaaa1905d195d9ce8e0a3b70e8381d6f9bc6ed56\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"path\": \"mcp/github.d.ts\",\n  \"listedBytes\": 674,\n  \"readBytes\": 674,\n  \"expectedUtf8Bytes\": 674,\n  \"contentChars\": 654,\n  \"hasNonAsciiDeclaration\": true,\n  \"ownerDocPresent\": true,\n  \"sameListReadBytes\": true,\n  \"bytesExceedChars\": true\n}\n```\n\n- Focused real Code Mode/QuickJS regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/code-mode.test.ts -t \"reports UTF-8 byte counts for MCP API files\"` — passed (2 tests, 120 skipped by the name filter).\n- Targeted formatting/lint/static checks: `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt.cmd --check src/agents/code-mode.worker.ts src/agents/code-mode.test.ts`, `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint.cmd src/agents/code-mode.worker.ts src/agents/code-mode.test.ts`, and `git diff --check` — all passed.\n- Fresh autoreview: `python .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings.",
